<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2789" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">antĕ-pīlānus</span></b> ,
			i, m.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In milit. lang. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>The soldiers who fought before the</i> pilani, i.
			e. <i>the hastati and the principes</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 8,
			8</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> In
			Ammianus, = antesignanus, <i>one who fought before the
				standards</i>, 16, 12, 20. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>a competitor</i>,
				<i>a rival</i>, <i><span class="en">Amm. 28,
			1</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
